description: CSS Modules — no class prefixes, states via data-*
alwaysApply: true
---

# CSS Modules

Modules already hash class names. Do not prefix classes with the component or element (`tab-icon`, `tab-active`). Parts are the thing they are. States are `data-*` attributes, nested with `&`.

## Parts

```css
/* Bad */
.tab-icon { }
.tab-label { }
.tab-close { }

/* Good */
.icon { }
.label { }
.close { }
```

```tsx
<span className={styles.icon} />
<span className={styles.label} />
```

Kebab-case for multi-word parts (`drag-spacer`, `new-tab`). Never camelCase.

## States

Boolean or mode variants are `data-*` on the element, never extra classes. Omit the attribute when false (`value || undefined`). Style with nested `&[data-x]`.

```tsx
<div
  className={styles.tab}
  data-active={active || undefined}
  data-pinned={pinned || undefined}
/>
```

```css
.tab {
  background: transparent;

  &[data-active] {
    background: var(--ds-background-primary);
  }

  &[data-pinned] {
    width: var(--tab-height);
  }

  &[data-pinned] .label {
    display: none;
  }
}
```

```css
/* Bad */
.tab-active { }
.tab-pinned .tab-label { }
```

Local tokens (`--tab-height`) may keep a short prefix. Class names may not.
